1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,177
Alcohols react at three places.

2
00:00:03,177 --> 00:00:07,656
The O H bond, where the hydrogen is weakly acidic.

3
00:00:07,656 --> 00:00:12,304
The carbon oxygen bond, where the O H is replaced or lost.

4
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:17,148
And the alpha carbon hydrogen bonds, which are attacked in oxidation.

5
00:00:17,148 --> 00:00:21,822
Keep this picture in mind, and every reaction falls into place.

6
00:00:21,822 --> 00:00:25,208
We will collect them all into one map as we go.

